<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <PlatformTarget>x64</PlatformTarget>
    <!--
      Exe, not WinExe. Exporter_studio's first job is a scan that reports, and a
      WinExe detaches from the console so every Console.WriteLine goes nowhere
      unless the app calls AllocConsole itself. An OpenTK GameWindow opens
      perfectly well from a console subsystem app, so the window this grows
      into does not need the switch flipped - it just keeps its log.
    -->
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <StartupObject>Program</StartupObject>
    <RootNamespace></RootNamespace>
    <OptionCompare>Text</OptionCompare>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>true</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
    <AssemblyName>Exporter_studio</AssemblyName>
    <!--
      OUTPUT GOES TO bin\<config>\ WHATEVER -p:Platform IS SET TO.

      MSBuild's default puts it in bin\<platform>\<config>\ as soon as
      Platform is anything but AnyCPU. CLAUDE.md tells every session to build
      nuTerra with -p:Platform=x64 - it needs it to resolve its C++ DLL - and
      that habit applied here quietly produced a SECOND exe in
      bind\Debug\, while the one nuTerra's find_exporter_studio() looks
      for in bin\<config>
et8.0-windows\ went stale. Two exes, the wrong one
      newer, and no error from either.

      This project is pure managed and sets PlatformTarget itself, so the
      platform never needed to be in the path. Pinning OutputPath means the
      flag is now harmless rather than something each person has to remember
      not to pass.
    -->
    <OutputPath>bin\$(Configuration)\</OutputPath>
    <!--
      For System.Drawing, which the UI font atlas rasterises through. This is
      the Windows Desktop SHARED FRAMEWORK, not a package: the project still
      carries exactly one PackageReference, which is what the one-dependency
      rule was protecting. The app was already net8.0-windows and x64, so it
      runs on exactly the machines it ran on before.
    -->
    <UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Same version nuTerra and SrtViewer pin, so all three agree on Vector3. -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTK" Version="4.7.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
